EXPERIMENT 18 – HTTP REQUEST DEFAULTS AND HEADER MANAGER USING APACHE JMETER

AIM
To use Apache JMeter to configure HTTP Request Defaults and HTTP Header Manager for REST API requests.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and create a Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 2, Ramp-up Period = 2 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add HTTP Request Defaults and enter the protocol and server name.
5. Add HTTP Header Manager with Content-Type and Accept as application/json.
6. Add two HTTP Request samplers: GET /posts/1 and GET /users/1.
7. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report listeners.
8. Run the plan and verify the JSON responses.
TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	2
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	2 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request Defaults	Protocol	https
HTTP Request Defaults	Server Name	jsonplaceholder.typicode.com
HTTP Header Manager	Content-Type	application/json
HTTP Header Manager	Accept	application/json
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	GET /posts/1
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	GET /users/1

